 ## Architectural content
 
+TopicMask is the immutable, neutral matching specification for a [Topic](9e2ffa9b4a1d4422a33c2a4bbcfc86ef.md).
+Feature-level selection, disclosure, publication, execution, persistence and
+routing decisions remain with their governed owners. Themis separately
+evaluates authorisation. A TopicMask has no runtime UUID and defines no
+natural order.
+
+### Kinds, structural equality and construction
+
+An ordinary mask contains one or more ordered TopicMaskEntry criteria and
+an `includeContainedElements` flag, false by default. Each criterion holds
+independent qualifier and value regular expressions and an optional version
+expression. Ordinary equality and hashing use the original expression strings
+in order, version-constraint presence and the containment flag.
+
+The universal kind explicitly matches every non-null Topic. All universal
+masks compare equal and hash consistently. Universal masks have no criteria,
+containment flag or ordinary canonical expression. Create one with
+`TopicMask.all()` or reconstruct it from its explicit logical kind. An ordinary
+mask remains ordinary even if it covers every valid Topic. An empty, invalid
+or ambiguous ordinary input never establishes universality. Ordinary-only
+accessors reject a universal mask.
+
+Build ordinary masks by appending validated immutable entries and setting
+containment. Successful builds return independent immutable snapshots.
+A failed addition or build preserves prior state. Builders remain reusable.
+Qualifier and value regex
+inputs must be supplied. Empty expressions are valid and cannot match the
+corresponding nonempty field. Validate literal helpers against completed
+TopicEntry field rules before quoting for RE2/J. A literal version, if supplied
+to a literal helper, must be valid and nonempty. Mask construction generates
+no default qualifier. It validates and compiles the original expressions
+within the release limits, including expressions produced by literal quoting.
+
+### Positional evaluation and version constraints
+
+`matches(Topic)` is a synchronous Boolean operation. A null candidate returns
+false for either kind. Check ordinary mask depth before evaluating any
+expression. Exact depth requires the same number of entries. Inclusive
+containment permits additional trailing entries. Match qualifier, value and
+any required version at each corresponding position, stopping on the first
+mismatch. Field evaluation uses full-field RE2/J matching on decoded text,
+case-sensitive by default and subject to supported expression flags. An
+expression cannot consume a different field or path position.
+
+| Version expression | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| Absent | Accept either version state for this field. |
+| Present but empty | Require a version; the empty expression fails against every valid present nonempty version. |
+| Present wildcard or other expression | Require a version and apply the supplied full-field expression to it. |
+
+Those states remain structurally distinct across comparison and serialization.
+Compile once at construction and share immutable patterns with per-call
+matching state. Enforce the release-defined depth, field and expression bounds
+and feasible complexity safeguards. Java regex fallback and a shared global
+match-result cache are excluded. Unexpected evaluation errors return false
+with safe ERROR diagnostics through the governed logger. Diagnostic failure
+cannot turn a mismatch or an evaluation error into a match. Invalid construction
+fails exceptionally and is logged at its handling boundary. Conditional TRACE
+and the error path use safe exit metadata. Buffering, backpressure, delivery
+and recovery belong to the logging framework. Its availability, bounded
+latency and reliability remain implementation evidence obligations.
+
+### Canonical expression and logical interchange
+
+An ordinary expression path uses `qualifierRegex[:versionRegex]=valueRegex`
+criteria separated by unescaped periods. Escape literal periods, equals
+signs, colons and backslashes in the original expression strings at the
+outer encoding layer. Decode exactly that layer before RE2/J validation.
+Preserve original expressions, including an explicit empty version constraint
+rendered with a colon immediately before the equals sign. Strict parsing
+rejects empty paths or segments, invalid escapes, extra or misplaced
+delimiters and invalid expressions. Round-trip an ordinary mask with its
+expression and separately supplied containment flag.
+
+Logical interchange carries the explicit mask kind. Ordinary records carry
+ordered criteria and containment and preserve absence versus a present
+empty expression. Universal records carry neither criteria nor containment
+and have no ordinary expression token. Reject ambiguous records, rebuild
+validated immutable masks and compile from the preserved expression text.
+Transport encoding is separate from the logical contract.
+
+### Governed reuse and historical references
+
+InformationUnitMask, OperationalMetadataMask and PetasosParcelMask compose
+or reference TopicMasks for governed Topic-valued criteria. Subscription,
+publication and filter statements compose their own criteria. Capability
+discovery, policy, routing and the other consumers retain their separate
+eligibility and selection rules. This primitive establishes no higher-mask
+catalogue, interpreter or consumer execution mechanism.
+
+Any governed persisted mask and historical identifier requires preservation
+or explicit migration under its boundary contract. Show criterion-basis and
+selection-scope equivalence before mapping Exact or Inclusive legacy selectors
+to depth flags or name-only selectors to positional criteria. Establish
+unrestricted intent before any conversion to the universal kind, validate the
+supported regex dialect, and fail closed on ambiguity. These are qualifications
+for governed data and boundaries.
+
